{"turn": 0, "t": 1794875179.7553828, "content": "", "tool_calls": [{"name": "get_search_space", "arguments": {}}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 881, "completion_tokens": 17, "seconds": 1.974442168}, "results": ["{\"space\": \"A RosaSeed configuration is a JSON object with exactly these fields:\\n- prechain: one of ['off', 't50w60', 't50w80', 't200w60', 't200w80']. Pre-chain singleton filter: 'off', or t<T>w<W> = once a read already has more than T chains, a seed shorter than W nt may not start a new singleton chain (less extension work, may lose alignments).\\n- frc: true/false. At the first pivot, look up both strands and keep the more specific one (one extra lookup per read).\\n- early_exit: true/false. Phase C gap filling stops at the first good seed in a gap instead of trying every pivot.\\n- k: integer 15..25. Minimum seed length (Phase C uses k+1). Larger = fewer, more specific seeds; faster but may miss alignments.\\n- cap: one of [50, 100, 200, 500, 1000, 2000, 5000]. Phase A skips seeds occurring more than cap times. Lower = faster, may miss seeds in repeats.\\n- gap: integer 1..15. Minimum uncovered read stretch that triggers a Phase C search.\\n- gap_step: integer 1..10. Step between Phase C pivot positions inside a gap.\\n\\nYOUR REGION (other values are rejected): {\\\"k\\\": {\\\"min\\\": 20, \\\"max\\\": 25}, \\\"cap\\\": [100, 200, 500], \\\"gap\\\": {\\\"min\\\": 5, \\\"max\\\": 10}, \\\"gap_step\\\": {\\\"min\\\": 5, \\\"max\\\": 10}}\\n\", \"budget_left\": 8}"]}
